%N A398788 Minimum number of rainbow spanning trees of K_n, over all JL-colorings.
%C A398788 A JL-coloring of a graph is an edge-coloring with (strictly) n-1 colors and no rainbow cycles, where n is the number of vertices. A rainbow spanning tree (cycle) is a spanning tree (cycle) in which every edge has a different color. K_n denotes the complete graph on n vertices.
%H A398788 Matthew DeVilbiss, Bradley Fain, Amber Holmes, Paul Horn, Sonwabile Mafunda, and K. E. Perry, <a href="https://ajc.maths.uq.edu.au/pdf/86/ajc_v86_p001.pdf">An extremal problem on rainbow spanning trees in graphs</a>, Australas. J. Combin., 86 (2023), 1-23.
%F A398788 a(n) = s*(n-s)*a(s)*a(n-s), where s is a power of 2 between n/3 and 2*n/3.
%o A398788 (Python)
%o A398788 import math
%o A398788 from functools import cache
%o A398788 @cache
%o A398788 def A(n):
%o A398788     if n == 2:
%o A398788         return 1
%o A398788     if n == 3:
%o A398788         return 2
%o A398788     # Calculate s = 2^(floor(log2(2n/3)))
%o A398788     s = 2 ** math.floor(math.log2(2 * n / 3))
%o A398788     return s * (n - s) * A(s) * A(n - s)
%Y A398788 Cf. A099396.
%K A398788 nonn,new
%O A398788 2,2
%A A398788 _Harry Richman_, Sep 05 2026
